SUMMARY:🌇 Sunset from Pebble Beach / Pier 1 (sun sets 6:42 pm)
LOCATION:
DESCRIPTION:\nhttps://mdunlap15.github.io/cousinnyctrip/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:nyc-2026-tatyana-d1-6-pcolonie@nyc
DTSTAMP:20260922T053139Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260927T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260927T211500
SUMMARY:🍽 Colonie
LOCATION:Colonie\, 127 Atlantic Ave\, Brooklyn\, NY 11201
DESCRIPTION:Elegant\, candlelit Atlantic Ave dining room with a living green wall — the natural dinner after sunset on the Brooklyn Heights Promenade.\nHours: Dinner nightly ~5:30–10\; brunch Sat–Sun\nPrice: $$$ (~$80pp)\nhttps://www.colonienyc.com\nhttps://mdunlap15.github.io/cousinnyctrip/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:nyc-2026-tatyana-d2-0-xrtowhitehall@nyc
DTSTAMP:20260922T053139Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260928T081000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260928T084500
SUMMARY:🚇 R from 4th Ave–9th St to Whitehall St (~30 min) — be at Battery security by 8:50
LOCATION:
DESCRIPTION:\nhttps://mdunlap15.github.io/cousinnyctrip/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:nyc-2026-tatyana-d2-1-pstatueofliberty@nyc
DTSTAMP:20260922T053139Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260928T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260928T130000
SUMMARY:🗽 Statue of Liberty (Liberty Island)
LOCATION:Statue of Liberty (Liberty Island)\, Liberty Island\, New York\, NY 10004 (ferries from Castle Clinton\, Battery Park)
DESCRIPTION:The first-timer icon: the ferry ride itself gives the classic skyline-and-harbor view\, and Liberty Island up close is genuinely moving. Combine with Ellis Island for a full half day.\nHours: Ferries from Battery Park ~9:00–9:30 first departure\, last outbound ~3:30pm\, last return ~5:30pm (fall schedule may shift)\nPrice: Ferry + grounds ~$25.50 adult\; Pedestal or Crown Reserve +$0.30 (includes Ellis Island)\nhttps://www.nps.gov/stli/\nhttps://mdunlap15.github.io/cousinnyctrip/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:nyc-2026-tatyana-d2-2-pwallstreetchargingbull@nyc
DTSTAMP:20260922T053139Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260928T133500
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260928T140000
SUMMARY:🗽 Wall Street\, Charging Bull & Fearless Girl
LOCATION:Wall Street\, Charging Bull & Fearless Girl\, Charging Bull: Bowling Green\, Broadway at Morris St\, New York\, NY 10004\; Fearless Girl: Broad St facing NYSE
DESCRIPTION:A 45-minute loop through the birthplace of the city: the bull (still at Bowling Green in 2026)\, Fearless Girl staring down the New York Stock Exchange\, Federal Hall where Washington was sworn in\, and Trinity Church's graveyard with Alexander Hamilton.\nHours: 24/7 (Federal Hall Mon–Fri 10–5\; Trinity Church daily)\nPrice: free\nhttps://www.downtownny.com/\nhttps://mdunlap15.github.io/cousinnyctrip/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:nyc-2026-tatyana-d2-3-ptinbuilding@nyc
DTSTAMP:20260922T053139Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260928T141600
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260928T152100
SUMMARY:🍽 Tin Building by Jean-Georges (South Street Seaport)
LOCATION:Tin Building by Jean-Georges (South Street Seaport)\, 96 South St\, New York\, NY 10038
DESCRIPTION:Jean-Georges Vongerichten's 53\,000 sq ft reconstruction of the old Fulton Fish Market: a gleaming food hall with a Chinese restaurant behind a hidden door\, a raw bar\, a French bistro and a very good grocery — with the Brooklyn Bridge right outside on Pier 17.\nHours: Daily roughly 8am–10pm (individual restaurants vary\; bars later)\nPrice: $$–$$$ (counter lunches $18–30\; sit-down dinner ~$80pp)\nhttps://www.tinbuilding.com/\nhttps://mdunlap15.github.io/cousinnyctrip/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:nyc-2026-tatyana-d2-4-p911memorial@nyc
DTSTAMP:20260922T053139Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260928T154000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260928T163000
SUMMARY:🗽 9/11 Memorial (reflecting pools)
LOCATION:9/11 Memorial (reflecting pools)\, 180 Greenwich St\, New York\, NY 10007
DESCRIPTION:Two acre-sized voids where the towers stood\, water falling into the footprints and 2\,983 names cut in bronze — quiet\, dignified and free. The Survivor Tree (a pear tree recovered from the rubble) stands nearby.\nHours: Daily 8am–8pm\nPrice: free\nhttps://www.911memorial.org/\nhttps://mdunlap15.github.io/cousinnyctrip/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:nyc-2026-tatyana-d2-5-xcoffeefidi@nyc
DTSTAMP:20260922T053139Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260928T164500
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260928T171000
SUMMARY:☕ Coffee break — La Colombe or Blue Bottle at Brookfield Place
LOCATION:
DESCRIPTION:\nhttps://mdunlap15.github.io/cousinnyctrip/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:nyc-2026-tatyana-d2-6-pbrooklynbridge@nyc
DTSTAMP:20260922T053139Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260928T173100
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260928T182600
SUMMARY:🚶 Brooklyn Bridge (pedestrian walk)
LOCATION:Brooklyn Bridge (pedestrian walk)\, Brooklyn Bridge Promenade\; Brooklyn stairs at Washington St & Prospect St\, Brooklyn\, NY 11201 / Manhattan entrance at Centre St & Park Row\, New York\, NY 10007
DESCRIPTION:The 1883 Gothic-arched bridge is the most beautiful walk in the city\; 1.1 miles of wooden promenade with the skyline\, harbor and Statue in view. Since 2021 the walkway is pedestrian-only (bikes moved to the roadway).\nHours: 24/7\nPrice: free\nhttps://www.nyc.gov/\nhttps://mdunlap15.github.io/cousinnyctrip/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:nyc-2026-tatyana-d2-7-pdumbowashingtonstreet@nyc
DTSTAMP:20260922T053139Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260928T184900
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260928T190400
SUMMARY:🗽 DUMBO — Washington Street viewpoint
LOCATION:DUMBO — Washington Street viewpoint\, Washington St between Front St & Water St (near 39 Washington St)\, Brooklyn\, NY 11201
DESCRIPTION:The cobblestone street that frames the Manhattan Bridge with the Empire State Building peeking through its arch — the most Instagrammed view in Brooklyn — surrounded by galleries\, Time Out Market\, Jacques Torres chocolate and the Empire Stores shops.\nHours: 24/7 (shops ~11am–7pm)\nPrice: free\nhttps://dumbo.nyc/\nhttps://mdunlap15.github.io/cousinnyctrip/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:nyc-2026-tatyana-d2-8-pcecconisdumbo@nyc
DTSTAMP:20260922T053139Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260928T191500
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260928T210000
SUMMARY:🍽 Cecconi's Dumbo
LOCATION:Cecconi's Dumbo\, 55 Water St\, Brooklyn\, NY 11201
DESCRIPTION:Soho House's glossy Venetian-style brasserie with a terrace facing the Brooklyn Bridge — the most scenic dinner in Brooklyn for a three-person evening.\nHours: Daily ~12–11\; brunch Sat–Sun\nPrice: $$$ (~$85pp)\nhttps://www.cecconisdumbo.com\nhttps://mdunlap15.github.io/cousinnyctrip/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:nyc-2026-tatyana-d3-0-pgrandcentralterminal@nyc
DTSTAMP:20260922T053139Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260929T104500
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260929T112500
SUMMARY:🗽 Grand Central Terminal
LOCATION:Grand Central Terminal\, 89 E 42nd St\, New York\, NY 10017
DESCRIPTION:The 1913 Beaux-Arts concourse with its turquoise zodiac ceiling is a landmark you can wander for free\, and it hides two of the best drinks stops in Midtown: The Campbell (1920s tycoon's office bar) and the Oyster Bar.\nHours: Daily 5:30am–2am\; shops/dining ~10am–9pm\nPrice: free\; official 90-min guided tour $39\nhttps://www.grandcentralterminal.com/\nhttps://mdunlap15.github.io/cousinnyctrip/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:nyc-2026-tatyana-d3-1-pstpatrickscathedral@nyc
DTSTAMP:20260922T053139Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260929T113600
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260929T120100
SUMMARY:🗽 St. Patrick's Cathedral
LOCATION:St. Patrick's Cathedral\, 5th Ave between E 50th & 51st St\, New York\, NY 10022
DESCRIPTION:James Renwick's 1879 Neo-Gothic cathedral facing Rockefeller Center — the spires against the glass towers are the classic Fifth Avenue photo\, and the restored interior is bright and calm after the sidewalk crowds.\nHours: Daily 6:30am–8:45pm\; Masses weekdays 7\, 7:30\, 8am\, noon\, 1pm\, 5:30pm\; Sun 7am–5:30pm hourly-ish (10:15am Solemn Mass)\nPrice: free (donation)\; audio guide extra\nhttps://saintpatrickscathedral.org/\nhttps://mdunlap15.github.io/cousinnyctrip/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:nyc-2026-tatyana-d3-2-prockefellercenter@nyc
DTSTAMP:20260922T053139Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260929T120500
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260929T123500
SUMMARY:🗽 Rockefeller Center
LOCATION:Rockefeller Center\, 45 Rockefeller Plaza (Channel Gardens at 5th Ave\, W 49th–50th St)\, New York\, NY 10111
DESCRIPTION:The Art Deco heart of Midtown: Prometheus over the sunken plaza\, the Channel Gardens\, Atlas facing St. Patrick's\, and Radio City's marquee around the corner. Top of the Rock\, Bar SixtyFive and the Rainbow Room are upstairs.\nHours: Plaza & concourse 24/7\; shops ~10am–8pm. The Rink opens Oct 10\, 2026 (after the trip)\; tree arrives Nov 7\nPrice: free to wander\nhttps://www.rockefellercenter.com/\nhttps://mdunlap15.github.io/cousinnyctrip/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:nyc-2026-tatyana-d3-3-plodi@nyc
DTSTAMP:20260922T053139Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260929T124500
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260929T135500
SUMMARY:🍽 Lodi
LOCATION:Lodi\, 1 Rockefeller Plaza\, New York\, NY 10020
DESCRIPTION:The Estela chef's chic Milanese café on the plaza at Rockefeller Center — cornetti\, tramezzini\, focaccia and a proper lunch that turns the Top of the Rock/St. Patrick's morning into something stylish instead of a chain sandwich.\nHours: Mon–Fri ~7:30am–9pm\; Sat–Sun from ~9am (confirm)\nPrice: $$ — pastries $6–8\, panini/salads $18–26\, pastas $28\nhttps://www.rockefellercenter.com/\nhttps://mdunlap15.github.io/cousinnyctrip/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:nyc-2026-tatyana-d3-4-pbergdorfgoodman@nyc
DTSTAMP:20260922T053139Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260929T141000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260929T153000
SUMMARY:🛍 Bergdorf Goodman
LOCATION:Bergdorf Goodman\, 754 Fifth Ave (at W 58th St)\, New York\, NY 10019
DESCRIPTION:The most beautiful department store in America: nine floors of the best women's designer edit in the city inside a 1928 mansion-style building facing the Plaza and Central Park. Even non-buyers come for the windows\, the 5th-floor contemporary floor and the shoe salon.\nHours: Mon–Sat 11am–7pm\, Sun 12–6pm (confirm)\nPrice: $$$$ (browsing free\; contemporary floor from ~$200\; BG Restaurant lunch ~$45–70pp)\nhttps://www.bergdorfgoodman.com/\nhttps://mdunlap15.github.io/cousinnyctrip/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:nyc-2026-tatyana-d3-5-pgoodmansbarbergdorf@nyc
DTSTAMP:20260922T053139Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260929T154000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260929T162500
SUMMARY:🍸 Goodman’s Bar at Bergdorf Goodman
LOCATION:Goodman’s Bar at Bergdorf Goodman\, 745 Fifth Ave (Bergdorf Goodman Men’s store\, lower level)\, New York\, NY 10151
DESCRIPTION:A sleek\, clubby Martini bar hidden in the basement of the men’s store across Fifth Avenue from the main Bergdorf — the chic way to recover from Fifth Avenue shopping.\nHours: Follows store hours: roughly Mon–Sat 11:30am–8pm\, Sun noon–6pm\nPrice: cocktails $22–26\; burger/caviar bites $25–60\nhttps://www.bergdorfgoodman.com/\nhttps://mdunlap15.github.io/cousinnyctrip/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:nyc-2026-tatyana-d3-6-ptopoftherock@nyc
DTSTAMP:20260922T053139Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260929T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260929T184000
SUMMARY:🗽 Top of the Rock
LOCATION:Top of the Rock\, 30 Rockefeller Plaza (entrance on W 50th St)\, New York\, NY 10112
DESCRIPTION:The best classic view in New York: Empire State Building straight ahead\, Central Park spread out behind you\, three open-air levels and no fences on the top tier. Our top pick of the five decks.\nHours: Daily 9am–midnight (last entry 11pm)\nPrice: General admission $40–61 by date (from ~$45)\; Beam combo from $73\; Skylift $35 add-on\; VIP from $207\nhttps://www.rockefellercenter.com/attractions/top-of-the-rock-observation-deck/\nhttps://mdunlap15.github.io/cousinnyctrip/
END:VEVENT
