BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:nyc-2026-tatyana-d4-0-plittleisland@nyc
DTSTAMP:20260922T053139Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260930T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260930T110000
SUMMARY:🌳 Little Island
LOCATION:Little Island\, Pier 55\, W 13th St & Hudson River Park\, New York\, NY 10014
DESCRIPTION:Barry Diller's tulip-pot island park on the Hudson: hilly paths\, an amphitheater\, and the best low-angle sunset over New Jersey — five minutes from the High Line start.\nHours: Daily 6am–11pm through Oct 31 (6am–9pm from Nov 1)\; weather closures possible\nPrice: free (no timed tickets needed)\nhttps://littleisland.org/\nhttps://mdunlap15.github.io/cousinnyctrip/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:nyc-2026-tatyana-d4-1-pwhitney@nyc
DTSTAMP:20260922T053139Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260930T111500
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260930T131500
SUMMARY:🖼 Whitney Museum of American Art
LOCATION:Whitney Museum of American Art\, 99 Gansevoort Street\, New York\, NY 10014
DESCRIPTION:MUST — Renzo Piano's building at the foot of the High Line has outdoor terraces over the Hudson and the best collection of 20th-century American art\; doing it on the free Friday night (Oct 2) at sunset\, then drinks in the Meatpacking District\, is the perfect evening.\nHours: Wed–Mon 10:30–6\, Fri 10:30–10\nPrice: $30 adults\; FREE Fri 5–10 pm and 2nd Sundays (ticket required)\; 25 and under free\nhttps://whitney.org/\nhttps://mdunlap15.github.io/cousinnyctrip/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:nyc-2026-tatyana-d4-2-pchelseamarket@nyc
DTSTAMP:20260922T053139Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260930T132500
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260930T142500
SUMMARY:🍽 Chelsea Market
LOCATION:Chelsea Market\, 75 9th Ave (between W 15th & 16th St)\, New York\, NY 10011
DESCRIPTION:The former Nabisco factory (where the Oreo was invented) is now the city's best-known food hall: Los Tacos No. 1\, The Lobster Place\, Very Fresh Noodles\, Li-Lac chocolates\, plus Artists & Fleas and Anthropologie for browsing.\nHours: Daily 7am–10pm (vendors vary\, most 11am–8pm)\nPrice: $ – $$ (tacos ~$5 each\, lobster ~$30)\nhttps://www.chelseamarket.com/\nhttps://mdunlap15.github.io/cousinnyctrip/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:nyc-2026-tatyana-d4-3-pthehighline@nyc
DTSTAMP:20260922T053139Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260930T143500
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260930T153000
SUMMARY:🚶 The High Line
LOCATION:The High Line\, Gansevoort St entrance\, 820 Washington St\, New York\, NY 10014 (runs to W 34th St)
DESCRIPTION:A 1.45-mile garden on an old freight railway with planting by Piet Oudolf\, art\, and glimpses into Chelsea galleries and Zaha Hadid's building — the most stylish free walk in the city.\nHours: Daily 7am–10pm (Apr 1–Nov 30)\nPrice: free\nhttps://www.thehighline.org/\nhttps://mdunlap15.github.io/cousinnyctrip/
END:VEVENT
