BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:nyc-2026-tatyana-d4-5-pbleeckerstreet@nyc
DTSTAMP:20260922T053139Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260930T164500
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260930T174000
SUMMARY:🛍 Bleecker Street (West Village)
LOCATION:Bleecker Street (West Village)\, Bleecker St between 6th Ave/Christopher St and Bank St\, New York\, NY 10014
DESCRIPTION:The West Village's postcard shopping street — brownstones\, Magnolia Bakery\, Marc Jacobs' Bookmarc\, Diptyque\, Cynthia Rowley — reborn after its 2017 vacancy slump with a mix of small fashion and home brands\, and the best restaurants of the trip (Via Carota\, Buvette) two blocks away.\nHours: Shops ~11am–7pm daily\; Magnolia to 10–11pm\nPrice: $$–$$$$ (Magnolia cupcake ~$5\; Diptyque candle ~$75)\nhttps://www.villagealliance.org/\nhttps://mdunlap15.github.io/cousinnyctrip/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:nyc-2026-tatyana-d4-6-pbarpisellino@nyc
DTSTAMP:20260922T053139Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260930T174300
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260930T182800
SUMMARY:🍸 Bar Pisellino
LOCATION:Bar Pisellino\, 52 Grove St (at 7th Ave S)\, New York\, NY 10014
DESCRIPTION:Rita Sodi and Jody Williams’ (Via Carota) tiny Venetian-style bar: espresso and cornetti in the morning\, spritzes and tramezzini from 4pm\, all at a marble counter or sidewalk tables.\nHours: Daily ~8am–midnight\nPrice: spritz $16–18\, cocktails $18–20\, pastries $6–9\nhttps://www.barpisellino.com/\nhttps://mdunlap15.github.io/cousinnyctrip/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:nyc-2026-tatyana-d4-7-plartusi@nyc
DTSTAMP:20260922T053139Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260930T183100
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260930T200600
SUMMARY:🍽 L'Artusi
LOCATION:L'Artusi\, 228 W 10th St\, New York\, NY 10014
DESCRIPTION:The polished\, buzzy West Village Italian that is easier to love than Carbone and easier to book: roasted mushrooms\, garganelli with ragù\, the olive oil cake\, a deep Italian wine list.\nHours: Dinner nightly from 5pm\; lunch/brunch Fri–Sun (confirm)\nPrice: $$$ — ~$90–110pp\; pastas $28–34\nhttps://www.lartusi.com/\nhttps://mdunlap15.github.io/cousinnyctrip/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:nyc-2026-tatyana-d4-8-pvillagevanguard@nyc
DTSTAMP:20260922T053139Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260930T201100
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260930T213100
SUMMARY:🎭 Village Vanguard
LOCATION:Village Vanguard\, 178 7th Ave S\, New York\, NY 10014
DESCRIPTION:The holy basement of jazz since 1935 — Coltrane\, Bill Evans and Sonny Rollins recorded here — and it still looks and sounds exactly like the album covers. The most authentic single hour of jazz in New York.\nHours: Nightly sets 8pm & 10pm (doors 7:30pm)\; Vanguard Jazz Orchestra every Monday\nPrice: ~$40 cover + one-drink minimum (drinks ~$15)\; cards accepted\nhttps://villagevanguard.com\nhttps://mdunlap15.github.io/cousinnyctrip/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:nyc-2026-tatyana-d5-0-pthemet@nyc
DTSTAMP:20260922T053139Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261001T101500
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261001T130000
SUMMARY:🖼 The Metropolitan Museum of Art (The Met Fifth Avenue)
LOCATION:The Metropolitan Museum of Art (The Met Fifth Avenue)\, 1000 Fifth Avenue\, New York\, NY 10028
DESCRIPTION:MUST — the one museum no first-timer skips: Temple of Dendur\, the European paintings\, the American Wing courtyard and the Costume Institute\; even three hours only scratches it\, so pick wings rather than trying to see everything.\nHours: Sun–Tue & Thu 10–5\, Fri–Sat 10–9\nPrice: $30 adults (NY State residents pay-what-you-wish)\nhttps://www.metmuseum.org/\nhttps://mdunlap15.github.io/cousinnyctrip/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:nyc-2026-tatyana-d5-1-pcafesabarsky@nyc
DTSTAMP:20260922T053139Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261001T131500
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261001T143000
SUMMARY:☕ Café Sabarsky (Neue Galerie)
LOCATION:Café Sabarsky (Neue Galerie)\, 1048 5th Ave (at E 86th St)\, New York\, NY 10028
DESCRIPTION:The most beautiful café in New York: a wood-panelled 1914 Vanderbilt mansion room with Bösendorfer piano\, Viennese coffee and real Sachertorte — a Hannover visitor will feel the European kinship instantly.\nHours: Reopens Thu Oct 1 2026: Mon 9–6\, Wed–Sun 9–9\, closed Tue (Neue Galerie galleries stay closed until Nov 12)\nPrice: $$ — coffee $6–8\, Sachertorte/strudel ~$12–14\, schnitzel lunch ~$35\nhttps://www.neuegalerie.org/cafesabarsky\nhttps://mdunlap15.github.io/cousinnyctrip/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:nyc-2026-tatyana-d5-2-pcentralpark@nyc
DTSTAMP:20260922T053139Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261001T150500
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261001T163000
SUMMARY:🌳 Central Park (south-end loop)
LOCATION:Central Park (south-end loop)\, Enter at Grand Army Plaza\, 5th Ave & E 59th St\, New York\, NY 10019 (or 72nd St & 5th Ave)
DESCRIPTION:The essential slow morning: the Mall's elm allée\, Bethesda Terrace\, Bow Bridge and a rowboat on the Lake are the postcard New York she has seen in every film. Early fall color usually starts in the first days of October.\nHours: Daily 6am–1am\; rowboats at the Boathouse daily 10am–5:30pm last rental (season through October\, weather permitting)\nPrice: free\; rowboats Mon–Thu $25/hr\, Fri–Sun $30/hr (card only)\, boats seat 4\nhttps://www.centralparknyc.org/\nhttps://mdunlap15.github.io/cousinnyctrip/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:nyc-2026-tatyana-d5-3-pmadisonavenue@nyc
DTSTAMP:20260922T053139Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261001T164800
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261001T174300
SUMMARY:🛍 Madison Avenue (Upper East Side)
LOCATION:Madison Avenue (Upper East Side)\, Madison Ave between E 57th and E 79th St (core 60th–72nd)\, New York\, NY 10021
DESCRIPTION:Quieter and more elegant than Fifth: fifteen blocks of townhouse boutiques where Upper East Side women actually shop — Hermès\, Celine\, Loro Piana\, Max Mara\, Prada\, Ralph Lauren's Rhinelander mansion — with Ladurée and Sant Ambroeus for the café stop.\nHours: Boutiques Mon–Sat 10/11am–6/7pm\, Sun 12–5/6pm (several closed Sun)\nPrice: $$$$ (Hermès\, The Row\, Loro Piana…)\; Ladurée macarons ~$4 each\nhttps://www.madisonavenuebid.org/\nhttps://mdunlap15.github.io/cousinnyctrip/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:nyc-2026-tatyana-d5-4-pbemelmansbar@nyc
DTSTAMP:20260922T053139Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261001T175700
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261001T190700
SUMMARY:🍸 Bemelmans Bar at The Carlyle
LOCATION:Bemelmans Bar at The Carlyle\, 35 E 76th St (at Madison Ave)\, New York\, NY 10021
DESCRIPTION:The most romantic room in New York: Ludwig Bemelmans’ 1947 “Madeline” murals\, gold-leaf ceiling\, tuxedoed waiters and a piano. The single best “we are in Manhattan” cocktail for two women who like style.\nHours: Daily from noon to ~12:30am\; live piano nightly from ~5:30pm\, trio/cover sets from ~9:30pm\nPrice: cocktails $28–34\; evening music cover ~$30–40 pp added from ~9:30pm (Mon–Sat)\nhttps://www.rosewoodhotels.com/en/the-carlyle-new-york\nhttps://mdunlap15.github.io/cousinnyctrip/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:nyc-2026-tatyana-d5-5-pjgmelon@nyc
DTSTAMP:20260922T053139Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261001T191400
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261001T202900
SUMMARY:🍽 J.G. Melon
LOCATION:J.G. Melon\, 1291 3rd Ave (at E 74th St)\, New York\, NY 10021
DESCRIPTION:The green-checked-tablecloth pub with watermelon knick-knacks and a top-3 New York burger — the unpretentious lunch after the Met or Madison Avenue shopping that every Upper East Sider swears by.\nHours: Daily ~11:30am–2am (kitchen later than most)\nPrice: $$ — burger ~$18\, cottage fries ~$9\; historically CASH ONLY (confirm)\nhttps://jgmelon-nyc.com/\nhttps://mdunlap15.github.io/cousinnyctrip/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:nyc-2026-tatyana-d6-0-plafayettegrandcafe@nyc
DTSTAMP:20260922T053139Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261002T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261002T104500
SUMMARY:☕ Lafayette Grand Café & Bakery
LOCATION:Lafayette Grand Café & Bakery\, 380 Lafayette St (at Great Jones St)\, New York\, NY 10003
DESCRIPTION:Andrew Carmellini's grand Parisian brasserie whose bakery window launched the viral Suprême — a round cream-filled croissant — and a great NoHo breakfast either way.\nHours: Bakery counter daily ~8am–5pm\; restaurant daily 8am–late (weekend brunch)\nPrice: Suprême croissant ~$9\, pastries $6–9\, brunch $$–$$$\nhttps://lafayetteny.com\nhttps://mdunlap15.github.io/cousinnyctrip/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:nyc-2026-tatyana-d6-1-psohoshopping@nyc
DTSTAMP:20260922T053139Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261002T105500
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261002T130500
SUMMARY:🛍 SoHo Shopping Walk
LOCATION:SoHo Shopping Walk\, Broadway\, Prince\, Spring\, Greene\, Mercer & Wooster Sts between Houston & Canal Sts\, New York\, NY 10012
DESCRIPTION:The densest shopping neighborhood in America under cast-iron facades and cobblestones: every brand a stylish 40-something wants has a SoHo store — from Uniqlo/Zara/Aritzia on Broadway to Khaite\, Ganni\, Mansur Gavriel and The RealReal on the side streets\, plus Chanel\, Dior and Vuitton on Greene.\nHours: Mon–Sat 10/11am–7/8pm\, Sun 11am–7pm\nPrice: free to stroll\; $–$$$$ inside (Uniqlo to Chanel)\nhttps://www.sohobroadway.org/\nhttps://mdunlap15.github.io/cousinnyctrip/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:nyc-2026-tatyana-d6-2-pbalthazar@nyc
DTSTAMP:20260922T053139Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261002T131500
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261002T142500
SUMMARY:🍽 Balthazar
LOCATION:Balthazar\, 80 Spring St\, New York\, NY 10012
DESCRIPTION:Keith McNally's 1997 recreation of a Paris grand brasserie — red banquettes\, mirrors\, the best people-watching room in SoHo. Breakfast here before shopping is the classic stylish-visitor move.\nHours: Mon–Fri 7:30am–midnight\; Sat–Sun brunch 9am–4pm\, dinner to midnight (confirm)\nPrice: $$$ — brunch ~$45pp\, dinner ~$95pp\; steak frites ~$46\, seafood tower ~$150\nhttps://www.balthazarny.com/\nhttps://mdunlap15.github.io/cousinnyctrip/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:nyc-2026-tatyana-d6-3-pelizabethstreetnolita@nyc
DTSTAMP:20260922T053139Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261002T143500
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261002T152000
SUMMARY:🛍 Elizabeth Street & Nolita
LOCATION:Elizabeth Street & Nolita\, Elizabeth St between E Houston St and Kenmare St (with Mott & Mulberry Sts)\, New York\, NY 10012
DESCRIPTION:The prettiest shopping walk in Manhattan for women in their 40s: low tenement blocks lined with the independent and French-girl brands — Sézane\, Clare V.\, Warm\, Love Adorned\, Le Labo — plus cafés every 50 metres and none of SoHo's chain-store crush.\nHours: Boutiques ~11am–7pm daily (Sun often 12–6)\nPrice: $$–$$$ (Sézane dresses ~$150–250\; Clare V. bags ~$200–500)\nhttps://www.nolitanyc.com/\nhttps://mdunlap15.github.io/cousinnyctrip/
END:VEVENT
