BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:nyc-2026-tatyana-d7-5-pbrooklynmuseum@nyc
DTSTAMP:20260922T053139Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261003T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261003T183000
SUMMARY:🖼 Brooklyn Museum
LOCATION:Brooklyn Museum\, 200 Eastern Parkway\, Brooklyn\, NY 11238
DESCRIPTION:MUST and 20 minutes from home — Iris van Herpen: Sculpting the Senses (140 haute-couture pieces\, to Dec 5) is the most style-relevant show in the city\, plus a top Egyptian collection and Judy Chicago's Dinner Party\; on Sat Oct 3 the free First Saturday party (5–11 pm) coincides with the opening of Art of Manga.\nHours: Wed–Sun 11–6\; First Saturday Oct 3 open 5–11 pm (free)\nPrice: $20 adults suggested (NYC residents pay-what-you-wish)\; Art of Manga $30 timed ticket\; Iris van Herpen requires a timed ticket\nhttps://www.brooklynmuseum.org/\nhttps://mdunlap15.github.io/cousinnyctrip/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:nyc-2026-tatyana-d7-6-polmsted@nyc
DTSTAMP:20260922T053139Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261003T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261003T205000
SUMMARY:🍽 Olmsted
LOCATION:Olmsted\, 659 Vanderbilt Ave\, Brooklyn\, NY 11238
DESCRIPTION:Greg Baxtrom's playful farm-to-table with a backyard garden where herbs are picked for your plate — one of Brooklyn's most loved dinners\, 15 minutes from Park Slope.\nHours: Dinner Wed–Sun ~5:30–10 (check)\; weekend brunch\nPrice: $$$ (~$90pp)\nhttps://www.olmstednyc.com\nhttps://mdunlap15.github.io/cousinnyctrip/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
